REGENT OF WEST BANGKA
REGIONAL REGULATION OF WEST BANGKA REGENCY
NUMBER 13 OF 2013
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION
FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF WEST BANGKA,
Considering : a. that children and women are creatures created by Almighty God who need to receive protection from violence for the sake of their dignity as human beings;
b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 5 of 1998 concerning Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1998 Number 164, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3783);
5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
7. Law Number 20 of 2003 concerning the National Education System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 78, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4301);
8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
9. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
10. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
11. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
12. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3495);
13. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
14. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning the Division of Government Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);
15. Regional Regulation of West Bangka Regency Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Authority of West Bangka Regency (Regional Gazette of West Bangka Regency of 2008 Number 1 Series D);
16. Regional Regulation of West Bangka Regency Number 15 of 2011 concerning Cooperation in the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Acts of Violence (Regional Gazette of West Bangka Regency of 2011 Number 2 Series E);
With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF WEST BANGKA REGENCY and

text:
BAB III
HAK-HAK KORBAN
Pasal 4
Setiap korban berhak mendapatkan:
a. perlindungan;
b. informasi;
c. pelayanan optimal;
d. penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap rehabilitasi;
e. penanganan secara rahasia;
f. pendampingan secara psikologis dan hukum; dan
g. jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan status korban sebagai  anggota keluarga maupun anggota masyarakat.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
Every victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal services;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. confidential handling;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and
g. guarantee of rights related to the victim's status as a family member as well as a member of society.

text:
BAB VI
LEMBAGA PENYELENGGARA PERLINDUNGAN TERHADAP KORBAN
Pasal 8
(1) Pemerintah Daerah membentuk Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu (PPT ) sebagai  Lembaga Penyelenggara, Pencegahan dan Perlindungan Perempuan dan  Anak Korban Kekerasan.
(2) PPT sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari unsur :
a. kesehatan;
b. penegak hukum;
c. sosial dan pemberdayaan;
d. pendidikan dan keagamaan;
e. Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat; dan
f. swasta.
(3) Ketentuan lebih lanjut tentang PPT sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTION FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS
Article 8
(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Implementing Institution for Prevention and Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.
(2) The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of:
a. health;
b. law enforcement;
c. social affairs and empowerment;
d. education and religious affairs;
e. Non-Governmental Organizations; and
f. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding the PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.
